# Media is committed as normal files so GitHub Pages can serve it directly.
# GitHub Pages does NOT resolve Git LFS pointers: an LFS-tracked video gets
# served as its ~130-byte pointer text instead of the file, so it won't play.
#
# Only files that exceed GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit are kept in Git LFS,
# because those cannot be pushed as normal files. If you add a new video over
# ~100 MB that needs to play on the site, compress it below 100 MB instead of
# adding it here.
media/clips/PolkRideCleanVers.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
media/clips/PolkRunRide.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
